# BUGS

Only the output firmware lit is used, at firmware's mode: no mode setting, hotplug, link training or transmitter, and the other engines are left dark.
Every flush copies the damage into a buffer of linlon's own, because without an IOMMU translating the engine's reads, a layer can only scan out memory contiguous in physical memory.
The engine's DMA goes through the stub's BTI, and its stream is in bypass on the display SMMU, so it could read all of memory.
The pixel format is XRGB8888 only, and no scaler, rotation, AFBC or second layer is used.
If linlon exits while an image is shown, the engine keeps scanning out its buffer, whose pages the kernel quarantines; nothing puts firmware's back.
